# Rift Project — AI Briefing Document

Read this every session. This is the single source of truth for how this project is organised.

---

## You Are Here

- **Local folder**: `~/Code/rift/`
- **Private GitHub repo**: `mkmk10k/rift-dev` (daily development, all source)
- **Public GitHub repo**: `mkmk10k/rift` (open-source mirror, MIT licence)

This is the **only folder you ever open for Rift work**. There is no reason to open any other folder.

---

## Directory Layout

```
~/Code/rift/
  src/                  Electron app — main, renderer, preload
  python/               ML scripts — STT/TTS servers, model download
  website/              myrift.dev static site (HTML/CSS/JS)
  scripts/
    release.js          Build DMG + publish GitHub Release to public repo
    publish-public.js   Sync curated source code to public repo
    bundle-python.js    Bundle Python runtime for distribution
    update-version.js   Auto-generate version from date + git hash
  test-engine/          Evals and automated tests
  tools/                Swift binaries for text injection / input switching
  setup/                First-launch Setup window HTML + assets
  input-method/         macOS Input Method extension (Swift)
  .cursor/rules/        AI rules — YOU are reading one now
  .cursor/skills/       AI skill files for complex tasks
  .gitignore            Covers node_modules, dist, models, credentials
  .publish-ignore       Defines what stays out of the public repo
```

---

## Git Remotes

| Remote | Repo | Visibility | When to use |
|--------|------|------------|-------------|
| `origin` | `mkmk10k/rift-dev` | **Private** | `git push` for all daily work |
| `public` | `mkmk10k/rift` | **Public** | NEVER push directly — use script |

```bash
git push origin main        # normal daily push — private
git push public main        # WRONG — always use bun run publish-public
```

---

## CRITICAL RULES — Never Break These

1. **NEVER `git push public` directly.** Always use `bun run publish-public`. The script enforces the `.publish-ignore` boundary. A direct push would expose internal tooling and the private website source.
2. **NEVER commit `.env`, models, or credentials** to any branch on either remote.
3. **`website/` is private.** It is excluded from the public repo by `.publish-ignore`. The website deploys separately via Cloudflare Pages.
4. **`scripts/release.js` is private.** Internal release tooling stays in the private repo.
5. **ML models are not committed.** `models/`, `Chatterbox-*/`, `python-bundle/` are gitignored and weigh 10–19GB.

---

## Key Commands

```bash
# Development
bun run dev                 # Start Electron app with hot reload

# Releasing
bun run release             # Build DMG + publish GitHub Release to mkmk10k/rift
bun run release:dry         # Preview release without publishing

# Public repo sync
bun run publish-public      # Sync curated source to mkmk10k/rift
bun run publish-public:dry  # Preview what would be synced

# Building without releasing
bun run package:dmg         # Build DMG only
bun run build               # TypeScript compile only

# Testing
bun run evals               # Full eval suite
bun run evals:quick         # LLM evals only
bun run evals:release       # Release gate (must pass before release)
```

---

## Website

- Source lives at `website/` inside this repo
- Deployed to **myrift.dev** via Cloudflare Pages (project name: `myrift-dev`)
- Deployment is **direct upload** (not GitHub-connected) — deploy with:
  ```bash
  bun run deploy:website
  ```
- This runs `wrangler pages deploy website/ --project-name myrift-dev`
- The separate `~/Code/myrift.dev/` folder is now **stale** — use `website/` instead

---

## Releases

- Releases (DMG files) are published to `mkmk10k/rift` (public repo) so download links work
- myrift.dev download buttons point to `github.com/mkmk10k/rift/releases/latest/download/...`
- Release script (`scripts/release.js`) explicitly uses `--repo mkmk10k/rift`
- After a release, run `bun run publish-public` to sync the source code too

---

## Public vs Private Boundary

What goes in the public `mkmk10k/rift` repo (defined by `.publish-ignore`):

| Public | Private (excluded) |
|--------|-------------------|
| `src/` — full app source | `website/` — marketing site |
| `python/` — ML scripts | `scripts/release.js` — internal tooling |
| `README.md`, `LICENSE`, `ROADMAP.md` | `.env*` — credentials |
| `DECISIONS.md`, `QUICKSTART.md`, `INSTALL.md` | `test-engine/reports/` — raw results |
| `test-engine/scenarios.ts` etc. | `test-engine/.cache/` — audio files |
| `package.json` (sanitised by rsync) | `.cursor/` — IDE config |

---

## Credentials and Signing

- Apple Developer credentials (for future notarization): store in `.env` or macOS Keychain
- `.env` is gitignored — never appears in either repo
- The app is currently **not notarized** (`identity: null` in package.json build config)
- Users must right-click → Open on first launch until notarization is set up
- When notarizing, needed env vars: `APPLE_ID`, `APPLE_APP_SPECIFIC_PASSWORD`, `APPLE_TEAM_ID`

